# Duskline — environment
#
# Every one of these is OPTIONAL. With none of them set the game runs fully:
# scores go to localStorage, guests get a local number, nothing is reported.
# Each one turns on a feature and says so honestly in the UI when it is off.
#
# Copy to .env.local for development. On Vercel, set them in
# Project → Settings → Environment Variables (and redeploy — env vars are
# baked into the client bundle at build time, not read at runtime).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared store, option A: Supabase  (takes precedence if both are set)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One-time setup: Supabase → SQL Editor → paste supabase/schema.sql → Run.
# Then copy from Project Settings → API (or let the Vercel Supabase
# integration set them):
#   SUPABASE_URL               the project URL, https://<ref>.supabase.co
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY  the service_role key (legacy, starts "eyJ"), or
#   SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY        a new secret key (starts "sb_secret_")
# SERVER-ONLY. Never prefix it NEXT_PUBLIC_: it bypasses row-level security.
# It powers everything the Upstash block below describes.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared store, option B: Upstash / Vercel KV
# Shared leaderboard + the guest number sequence
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without these, /api/scores keeps scores in per-instance memory — which on
# serverless means they effectively vanish — and the GLOBAL tab says "shared
# board activates once a KV store is connected". Guests get a random local
# number instead of the next one in a real sequence.
#
# The SAME store now also holds a signed-in player's synced profile
# (/api/profile: settings, career, any season in progress). Without it, sync
# answers `{synced: false, reason: "no-store"}` and the home screen says the
# profile is saved on this device — see src/ui/sync.ts. That route needs the
# Google client id below as well: it is keyed by the Google subject id and
# every call is verified, so there is nothing to key by without one.
#
# Easiest source: Vercel Marketplace → Upstash Redis (free tier is ample).
# Adding it from the Vercel dashboard sets these for you automatically.
# The UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_* pair is accepted as an alias.
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sign-in with Google  (optional; guest is always available)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Identity Services, which needs only the PUBLIC client id — no secret,
# no callback URL, no session store. Create one at
# console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials → OAuth client ID
# → Web application, and add your deployment origin to "Authorised JavaScript
# origins". Unset, the Google button on the sign-in gate is disabled and says
# it is not configured.
#
# It is also what /api/profile checks `aud` against. That check is the whole
# of the route's authorisation: without it the server would accept a perfectly
# valid Google token minted for somebody else's application, and anyone who
# learned a subject id could overwrite that player's career. So sync stays off
# entirely until this is set — see src/server/googleAuth.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Crash reporting  (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A Sentry DSN. It is a public credential — it is meant to ship in the client
# bundle. See src/ui/report.ts: this posts the ingest envelope directly rather
# than pulling in the ~90 kB Sentry SDK. Unset, crashes only reach the console.
# Reports carry the error, the stack, the realm/mode/car and the GPU string.
# They never carry a player name.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Score verification  (optional, recommended once the board is shared)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any random string of 16+ characters. With it set, /api/scores refuses any
# submission that does not carry a server-issued race ticket — one issued when
# a race STARTS, checked against the claimed duration, and valid for exactly
# one score. Without it, posting works as before and the API reports
# `verified: false` rather than implying a guarantee it is not making.
#
# It does NOT make scores trustworthy: the client still computes them. What it
# closes is `curl` with a believable number and no race. See
# src/server/raceToken.ts.
RACE_TOKEN_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dev only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lets /api/devpreview write realm preview JPEGs into public/previews. Refuses
# to run in production regardless. Only set this while regenerating previews.
FR_ALLOW_PREVIEW_WRITE=
